From 26a58a840433bad319a20c0287e5a9f2aa1faf57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LegendaryFire <tristan.balon@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:42:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Share Inkling 2's VRAM between its experts and its cache
 windows

A layer's experts all stayed in VRAM, so a long context's caches did
not fit beside them and decode read most of the cache from RAM. Now
every expert is also in pinned RAM and VRAM holds those the pool keeps
there (slabs of 4, one allocation each): the GPU groups a layer's
routed entries by the experts it holds, CPU threads compute the others
from the GPU's q8_1 activations as its grouped kernels do (SITU, the
product re-quantized, down), at the same time; a prompt chunk copies
the missing experts in, 16 a batch into one half of a staging area
while the GPU runs the other. Same products as with every expert in
VRAM (greedy tokens identical at 64, 0 and 128 experts in VRAM).

--kv-resident auto is the pool: each session's full-attention window
starts at a prompt chunk plus the bias range and grows as the session
does, by rebuilding its ring from the RAM copy; the least-used experts
on the card (routings a byte, counted on the GPU) give it their slabs.
A session that starts over shrinks back and the room goes to the
most-used experts in RAM, and every 4 steps up to 8 experts a card in
RAM worth 1.25x a resident one of their size take its slot, copied in
the background (the CPU computes them until the copy is done). The
routing is skewed (a layer's most-used half of the experts takes 88%
of its routings): with 2247 of 3072 experts in VRAM 96.6% of routings
hit, 8K decode 38.2 tok/s against 44 with all of them. Forwards hold the pool's lock shared,
so nothing in flight reads a moved expert. --vram-reserve-mib is the
VRAM it leaves free on a card; --experts-vram N pins N a layer.

2x RTX 3060, UD-Q4_K_XL, one session, decode without drafting:
128K 16.4 -> 29.7 tok/s, 256K 9.3 -> 22.2, 500K 5.2 -> 14.8 (a 64K
window before; now all 520K cells in VRAM beside 1788 of 3072
experts). Short contexts keep every expert: 8K decode 44.4 vs 44.6.
